\f1\i0  PAPER \'85 but something went wrong with the hand-off, didn\'92t it?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones let his lower jaw grind left and right while his particle pistol never wavered from its target. He surveyed the mansion grounds beyond the gate, even though he knew how many tanks were deployed there. He commanded enough fire power hovering above the Layer to neutralise them, but he\'92d prefer to resolve this via hand-to-hand grisliness if it came to violence. He loved to watch the light go out in an enemy\'92s eyes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley pressed on. \'91It all makes sense. It was Jacobson\'92s first day at her new job. Supaporn\'92s just a cleaner contracted in for crime scenes. They were both innocent bystanders who got caught in your operational tax-up.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The corner of Agent Jones\'92 mouth may have curled up a little\'97Hayley wasn\'92t sure, but she took it to mean he wanted her to know he couldn\'92t be baited.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You will come with me,\'92 Agent Jones told Hayley. \'91And Jacobson and Supaporn will surrender,\'92 he added, now he was sure Jacobson and the cleaner were holed up on the property.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Hey, sport,\'92 Kathy said while she drew an arc on the ground with her toe. \'91You see those tanks in there? They\'92re not just toys, you know.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Little beetles,\'92 Agent Jones said, \'91With tiny parasites crawling inside.\'92 He snapped his fingers.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The congregation of Elvi and accomplices seemed to know to hold their breath until something happened. It started with increasing volume of the thrum from the sky. A small swarm of gunships descended under the Layer, and hung there like enormous blowflies under a green sheep\'92s belly.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I have the tactical advantage,\'92 Agent Jones said and fixed a smile across his face. Hayley thought this was as much fun as the PAPER agent allowed himself.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Excuse me, agent,\'92 a foppish male voice came from stage left. \'91You appeared to have wandered onto my set. Could you please go and sign in at the visitor\'92s trailer?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I am here on a matter of national security,\'92 Agent Jones said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I\'92m here on a matter of national entertainment,\'92 Alexander countered, \'91and I think you know which national matter takes precedence.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91By who\'92s authority?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91If you know who I am\'97and I think you do know who I am because, let\'92s face it: who doesn\'92t?\'97then you would know by whose authority.\'92 Alexander hated to play the 
\f2\i Mother
\f1\i0  card, but not nearly as much as he loved playing the 
\f2\i Mother
\f1\i0  card.  While it diminished his personal potency, it was hard to eschew the look of terror that illuminated the eyes of all the other gamblers at the table.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Alexander Koalemos,\'92 Agent Jones said through clenched teeth, deliberately omitting Alexander\'92s fictitious rank of lieutenant.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Very well, then,\'92 Alexander went on with a self-satisfied 
\f2\i it\'92s-good-to-be-king
\f1\i0  kind of demeanour. \'91If you like, you\'92re welcome to stand over there with the other Randies while we \'85 start \'85 shooting.\'92 Alexander framed a silent 
\f2\i Bang!
\f1\i0  with his mouth, and smiled in a way that would cause every human being who ever existed to want to wipe it off his face with their bare knuckles.\

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Supercilious prat
