<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones seethed. The heat rising from him would\'92ve broken infrared instruments for kilometres around. Hayley couldn\'92t tell if Alexander was deliberately baiting the PAPER agent, or if he was genuinely that stupid. Whatever the reason, Hayley enjoyed watching it from third person for a change. Kathy seemed amused too. They exchanged a look.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Okay, camera team six, you\'92re with me,\'92 Alexander called out and waved a non-specific group his way. He started for the gates. \'91Come on, supporting cast,\'92 he said to Hayley, Kathy and the guards. \'91We\'92ve got some serious investigative storytellin\'92 to do.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re not going in,\'92 Kathy warned Alexander as the guard formed a blockade before the gates.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Thank my tax angels,\'92 Hayley said as she strode alongside Kathy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy stopped and fixed Hayley with a gaze. \'91You either.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 Hayley protested. \'91I\'92m on their side.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sorry,\'92 Kathy said, much gentler than the circumstance may have required. \'91In another time, another place \'85\'92 She made a regretful grimace.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander turned back. \'91Ah, Agent Jones! On reflection, I think what this stage of the story requires is a raising of the stakes \'85 a little more action, shall we say? I wonder if you\'92d consider being written in at this point. I\'92d be happy to allow you and your team a \'85 a reasonably free level of improvisational license.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones grinned like a gremlin. Into his wrist device, he said, \'91You will bring them down.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The PAPER gunships grew ominously larger and louder in the sky.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Okay, okay,\'92 Kathy soothed. \'91Come with me. And stay close. You too, Inspector Lanning. But no camera crew!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander thought on that a moment. \'91Okay we can make that work. I have the best scene reconstruction team in the country, you know.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I did not know that,\'92 Kathy said so genuinely and sympathetically, Alexander crest-fell almost to his knees.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Some people care nothing for art,\'92 Alexander mumbled as the three of them passed through the gates, flanked on both sides by Elvi guards.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones grinned with grim anticipation, as he watched his gunships land. While he may not be watching the lights go out in anyone\'92s eyes today, there remained a plethora of savorous, second-best options available.
